; beancount's inventory keys a lot by its cost's value, so 100 USD and
; 100.00 USD on one date are one lot, and each addition stores the
; position anew with its own cost: the lot holds the number the latest
; addition wrote, and a reduction books, prints and weighs at that number,
; whatever its own spec states. Within one transaction a posting reduces
; only what the account held before it, so two postings of opposite sign
; at one cost are both additions, the last of which sets the number.
2020-01-01 open Assets:A
2020-01-01 open Assets:B
2020-01-01 open Assets:C
2020-01-01 open Assets:D
2020-01-01 open Assets:Cash
2020-01-01 open Equity:O
2020-01-01 open Income:Gains

2020-01-02 * "A: 100 then 100.00"
  Assets:A  10 HOOL {100 USD}
  Assets:A  10 HOOL {100.00 USD}
  Assets:Cash  -2000 USD

2020-01-03 * "A: reduces at 100.00"
  Assets:A  -5 HOOL {100 USD}
  Income:Gains

2020-01-04 * "A: augmented again, at 100.0"
  Assets:A  1 HOOL {100.0 USD, 2020-01-02}
  Assets:Cash  -100 USD

2020-01-05 * "A: reduces at 100.0"
  Assets:A  -5 HOOL {}
  Income:Gains

2020-01-06 * "B: 100.00 then 100"
  Assets:B  10 HOOL {100.00 USD}
  Assets:B  10 HOOL {100 USD}
  Assets:Cash  -2000 USD

2020-01-07 * "B: reduces at 100"
  Assets:B  -5 HOOL {100.00 USD}
  Income:Gains

2020-01-08 * "C: in one transaction, nothing held before, neither posting reduces"
  Assets:C  10 HOOL {100.00 USD}
  Assets:C  -1 HOOL {100 USD}
  Equity:O

2020-01-09 * "C: reduces at 100, the last addition's number"
  Assets:C  -1 HOOL {100 USD}
  Income:Gains

2020-01-08 * "D: the short lot first, then the long"
  Assets:D  -1 HOOL {100 USD}
  Assets:D  10 HOOL {100.00 USD}
  Equity:O

2020-01-09 * "D: reduces at 100.00"
  Assets:D  -1 HOOL {100 USD}
  Income:Gains
